<title>USA: Phil. Exchange to trade oil service co options.</title>
<headline>Phil. Exchange to trade oil service co options.</headline>
<dateline>PHILADELPHIA 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philadelphia Stock Exchange will start trading options on the oil service sector from February 24.</p>
<p>The exchange said in a statement that its sector would comprise a price weighted index of 15 oil service companies.</p>
<p>The 15 are Baker Hughes Inc, Cooper Cameron Corp, Dresser Industries Inc, Falcon Drilling Co Inc, Global Industries Ltd, Global Marine Inc, Halliburton Co, Noble Drilling Corp, Reading &amp; Bates Corp, Rowan Cos Inc, Schlumberger Ltd, Smith International Inc, Tidewater Inc, Transocean Offshore Inc and Varco International Inc. ((-- New York Newsroom 212 859 1902))</p>
</text>
